00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:26.160
The case on both sides of narrowing Metro Vancouver turns on a conservative platform promise,

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:27.300
Daily High Reports.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:33.600
Lauren Dorkson's BC Conservatives say that if they win on October 24, the regional district

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:37.980
would lose housing, economic development, air quality, and climate policy.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:42.000
Bulk drinking water in sewage treatment would remain for local governments.

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:46.720
Those two utilities already make up most of the regional operating and capital budgets.

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:51.780
Carson Binda, the conservative candidate for Vancouver Quilchena, called the present

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:56.440
body not a utility, but an unaccountable bureaucratic mess with a blank check.

00:04:56.940 --> 00:05:02.100
He said conservatives would take the checkbook back, focus Metro on water and sewage, and

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:04.420
make sure taxpayers get value for every dollar.

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:09.860
The party says consultant and contractor costs now exceed in-house salaries and benefits.

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:14.780
It cites growing debt in the operating budget, and argues the province and municipalities

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:19.580
should take the other four services because that work duplicates what they already do.

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:24.880
Lynn Block, the candidate for North Vancouver Seymour, said a smaller professional board

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:27.800
will run this utility like the essential service it is.

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:34.100
The board itself in July 2026 asked the province to allow a 25% cut in directors.

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:40.460
Directors now come from 21 municipalities, electoral area A and the Tawassen First Nation.

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:45.420
On the North Shore Waste Water Treatment Plant, Trevor Withers, the candidate for North

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:50.460
Vancouver Lawnsdale, said people want clean water and working sewers, not a regional

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:54.220
bureaucracy that can't build a plant on budget and never answers for it.

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:59.740
Caroline Elliott, the candidate for West Vancouver Capillano, said conservatives would audit

00:05:59.740 --> 00:06:02.920
what went so disastrously wrong under the NDP's watch.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:08.900
Construction began in 2017 at about $700 million, then aimed at 2020.

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:14.760
The expected cost is now about $3.9 billion dollars with completion in 2030.

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:17.860
Households are seeing upward pressure on user fees.

00:06:18.280 --> 00:06:21.000
The district restarted an independent review this summer,

00:06:21.220 --> 00:06:24.200
with a final report expected in early 2027.

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:27.980
A May 2025 Deloitte review, done with the province,

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:32.080
has already led to stronger internal auditing and changes to board pay.

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:38.840
